<title>CHINA: Shanghai labour disputes increase in 1996.</title>
<headline>Shanghai labour disputes increase in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai experienced 3,166 labour disputes between companies and individual employees in 1996, a 24 percent increase over 1995, the Shanghai-based Business News said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said 40 percent of the disputes occurred in state-owned enterprises and 34 percent in foreign-funded firms with a third of all cases resulting from employment contracts being terminated and another third relating to salary disputes.</p>
<p>A total of 87 percent of the cases went to court of which 27 percent were won by the companies and 37 percent by employees, it said.</p>
</text>
